WEBVTT

00:21.040 --> 00:23.580
That laughter is disgusting as usual.

00:23.790 --> 00:26.540
<i>This is Nico's mother, Ibuki Wakatsuki.</i>

00:27.130 --> 00:29.090
I'm going to succeed this time.

00:29.960 --> 00:32.920
<i>She specializes in prophetic magic.</i>

00:33.420 --> 00:34.880
136.

00:36.050 --> 00:42.640
7, 1, 79, 4, 1.

00:38.050 --> 00:40.930
<i>The numbers that the book whispers
are page number,</i>

00:40.930 --> 00:43.850
<i>line number, and word number
from the top of the line.</i>

00:43.980 --> 00:46.730
<i>Then, by putting together
those appointed words,</i>

00:46.730 --> 00:49.150
<i>the prophecy statement can be formed.</i>

00:54.280 --> 00:57.200
Dog and... Raindrop...

00:58.160 --> 00:59.490
will bring disaster.

02:30.620 --> 02:35.000
<b>FRESH TRANSPARENT FASHIONS FOR SPRING</b>

02:34.670 --> 02:36.760
<i>If the coffee beans are fresh,</i>

02:37.050 --> 02:38.630
<i>and you pour hot water over them,</i>

02:38.630 --> 02:42.600
<i>it'll puff up like a hamburger patty
and a beautiful, rich scent will hit your nose.</i>

02:43.180 --> 02:45.890
<i>You pour 16 parts hot water
to one part coffee grounds.</i>

02:46.560 --> 02:51.770
<i>My favorite mug got broken the other day,
but I received a new one.</i>

02:52.230 --> 02:53.900
<i>It's inexpensive, but I like it a lot.</i>

02:54.860 --> 02:58.240
<i>A quiet moment in the morning
is a crucial part of my routine.</i>

02:58.650 --> 03:02.530
<i>I'm really happy when I get to enjoy
this moment on my weekends.</i>

03:02.740 --> 03:04.030
Good morning!

03:09.620 --> 03:10.920
<i>So, what do you think, Moi?</i>

03:11.250 --> 03:14.000
<i>Your roommate's
just-out-of-bed pajama outfit.</i>

03:14.130 --> 03:17.170
<i>A vulnerable sexiness,
but with an innocent cuteness.</i>

03:17.170 --> 03:20.670
<i>Fill your brain with the morning you can spend
with this sexy and charming young woman!</i>

03:20.930 --> 03:21.760
Hmmph.

03:21.760 --> 03:22.930
<i>Such a blank face.</i>

03:23.300 --> 03:26.180
<i>You're kidding, right? What's with him?
You're supposed to say something like,</i>

03:26.180 --> 03:30.270
<i>"Whoa there, don't wander around the house
like that, hurry up and go change"?</i>

03:30.270 --> 03:31.940
Oh, you're awake.

03:31.940 --> 03:36.480
<i>What the hell? You're living under a roof
with a girl, and that's what you say?</i>

03:36.480 --> 03:40.280
Just because it's the weekend doesn't mean
you can be lazy, so go change.

03:40.690 --> 03:42.780
<i>Okay, Mom.</i>

03:43.990 --> 03:46.410
That said, you always
seem to wear similar outfits.

03:51.870 --> 03:54.040
They do kind of look the same.

03:54.250 --> 03:56.210
They're all old linen smocks,

03:56.210 --> 03:59.630
but it felt like I had a lot because
they're all different colors with different details.

03:59.630 --> 04:02.550
But if other people look at them,
they're all basically the same, huh?

04:03.590 --> 04:07.050
And nowadays, high school girls
are so fashionable.

04:07.430 --> 04:12.390
Kara gave me some magazines,
but I don't have cute clothes like this.

04:12.390 --> 04:14.230
It's no wonder Moi
would give me a blank stare.

04:14.230 --> 04:15.060
Hmmmph.

04:15.350 --> 04:18.320
I think I should put some effort
into looking fashionable.

04:20.280 --> 04:21.690
Effort, huh?

04:22.110 --> 04:23.950
Effort...

04:24.410 --> 04:25.570
Effort.

04:26.660 --> 04:28.200
Or I could use that spell.

04:28.200 --> 04:30.790
<i>She decided to use magic instead!</i>

04:31.200 --> 04:33.870
Pulp Fashion!

04:34.170 --> 04:38.840
<i>This spell reproduces an outfit
from a picture.</i>

04:40.420 --> 04:43.090
Nice, this looks pretty fashionable.

04:43.550 --> 04:46.840
<i>However, since pictures
only show one side of the outfit,</i>

04:47.140 --> 04:50.060
<i>the other side of the outfit is see-through.</i>

04:51.390 --> 04:53.730
Really, what's up with this spell?

04:53.730 --> 04:56.100
I just have to be careful
not to show the back side.

04:56.310 --> 05:01.150
Because if that happens,
my romantic adolescence will be over.

05:01.530 --> 05:03.400
But maybe I do want him to see it.

05:03.400 --> 05:04.490
Just the front.

05:04.490 --> 05:05.820
Okay, let's go.

05:06.070 --> 05:09.370
I have to show him the feminine charms
of today's women!

05:15.460 --> 05:16.420
What's wrong, Nico?

05:16.420 --> 05:17.960
- Don't look!
- What?

05:17.960 --> 05:20.840
Oh, this is um,
training for walking sideways!

05:20.840 --> 05:21.800
Why?

05:22.170 --> 05:24.880
First, you put your palms together.

05:25.550 --> 05:27.130
And then you use that
to push into motion!

05:27.130 --> 05:28.180
Chairman Netero?

05:31.890 --> 05:34.810
<i>He cannot take her six o'clock.</i>

05:34.890 --> 05:40.440
<i>Nico's concentration was like that of a wrestler
on the glorious Olympic stage.</i>

05:41.070 --> 05:42.440
I think I'll get seconds.

05:43.980 --> 05:45.820
- Sexual harassment!
- Why?!

05:45.990 --> 05:47.820
Just please do not move.

05:47.820 --> 05:49.410
Sit down and stay.

05:49.410 --> 05:51.580
Huh? Uh, sure.

05:59.380 --> 06:00.710
Hey dude, what'cha got!

06:00.960 --> 06:02.710
- Are you taking my food order?
- No!

06:02.840 --> 06:05.550
This! My clothes! Don't make me say it.

06:05.550 --> 06:06.550
Oh.

06:06.550 --> 06:08.380
It looks nice.

06:08.680 --> 06:10.930
I didn't know you had clothes like that.

06:11.010 --> 06:12.220
<i>Only half, though.</i>

06:12.510 --> 06:14.100
Oh, I see.

06:14.520 --> 06:17.430
You wanted to dress up and go outside?

06:17.640 --> 06:18.940
All right, let's head out.

06:18.940 --> 06:20.230
- Are you crazy?
- What?

06:20.230 --> 06:22.270
You want me to go outside like this?
Are you nuts?

06:22.270 --> 06:24.360
What? Did I say something weird?

06:25.230 --> 06:30.240
No, I just wanted you to see.

06:31.450 --> 06:32.620
I got it.

06:33.030 --> 06:36.200
But I like the way you normally dress, too.

06:37.120 --> 06:41.790
Those kinds of clothes are nice, too,
but your usual ones have a nice, soft feel to it.

06:42.080 --> 06:45.630
But more than anything, I think people
look best in clothes that they like wearing.

06:49.340 --> 06:51.140
I-I'm gonna go change!

07:00.060 --> 07:02.980
Are those kinds of clothes
popular these days?

07:03.940 --> 07:07.490
Of course not! Please don't look!

07:13.120 --> 07:14.870
Yeah, that looks nice.

07:16.450 --> 07:19.120
It looks really great. My heart is racing.

07:20.370 --> 07:21.120
Yay!

07:21.710 --> 07:24.340
<i>I thought Moi
was more of the quiet, stoic type,</i>

07:24.340 --> 07:27.380
<i>but he'll actually compliment you honestly.</i>

07:27.380 --> 07:29.880
<i>Oh, I just love him so much.</i>

07:30.630 --> 07:31.510
Huh?

07:31.880 --> 07:33.430
Can I take a closer look?

07:35.350 --> 07:36.510
Sure.

07:44.020 --> 07:46.020
<i>Is he going to kiss me?</i>

07:47.780 --> 07:49.570
The detailed gathers...

07:50.440 --> 07:53.740
The way that it swishes and drapes
that's specific to old linen fabric...

07:55.120 --> 07:57.620
What era is this vintage smock from?

07:57.620 --> 07:58.540
Era?

07:59.120 --> 08:01.910
Huh? I-I don't really know,

08:01.910 --> 08:07.090
but all my clothes are hand-me-downs
from my French great-grandmother.

08:07.090 --> 08:08.420
I knew it!

08:08.420 --> 08:13.300
Looking at the fabric, I surmised
that it was something from the 1920s.

08:13.300 --> 08:14.550
Do you know how valuable it is?

08:14.550 --> 08:15.470
Whoa?

08:15.470 --> 08:18.060
So your heart has been racing because...

08:18.260 --> 08:20.470
I love old European clothing.

08:20.470 --> 08:22.310
A surprise vintage clothing nerd!

08:22.640 --> 08:24.270
It's really fantastic.

08:24.270 --> 08:26.230
Especially France's vintage clothing
is the best.

08:26.230 --> 08:28.230
Silhouette, feel of the fabric,
and the details.

08:28.230 --> 08:31.280
They all have something to it that
can't be reproduced in the current times.

08:31.280 --> 08:32.780
Yeah, it's simply the best.

08:32.780 --> 08:34.200
Look at him go!

08:34.320 --> 08:36.490
By the way, this jacket that I wear a lot

08:36.490 --> 08:39.490
is actually a 1940s Adolphe Lafont
moleskin jacket.

08:39.490 --> 08:41.200
A what now?

08:41.290 --> 08:43.410
I can't believe you.

08:43.410 --> 08:47.380
Your heart racing for clothes...
You saw my butt, you know.

08:47.590 --> 08:48.540
Hmmmmph.

08:48.540 --> 08:50.000
And there's that face!

08:51.210 --> 08:53.220
I saw that it was see-through,

08:53.380 --> 08:55.720
but I couldn't really see anything else
because of the light's reflection.

08:55.930 --> 08:57.760
Plus a trash can
came flying at me pretty quickly.

08:58.970 --> 09:02.470
<i>I'm glad he didn't see anything, but it
makes me mad that he's so calm about it.</i>

09:02.680 --> 09:05.690
So you just don't have
any interest in other people, right?

09:05.690 --> 09:08.730
Even though we live together,
it's almost like I'm not here.

09:08.730 --> 09:09.770
That's not true.

09:10.320 --> 09:13.740
It is! You probably prefer
spending time by yourself.

09:13.740 --> 09:16.030
You probably thought it got rowdy
when I started living here.

09:16.450 --> 09:17.950
That part is true.

09:19.160 --> 09:21.790
<i>Hmph, I can't believe this guy.</i>

09:21.790 --> 09:24.160
<i>I'm just not gonna talk to him
for the rest of the day.</i>

09:25.080 --> 09:27.790
Growing up, it was just me and my dad.

09:29.340 --> 09:33.510
So I've come to find out that
when it gets rowdy, it's not so bad.

09:35.800 --> 09:37.090
I see.

09:37.590 --> 09:39.640
Just wear clothes
that are comfortable for you.

09:39.970 --> 09:42.010
But those clothes from before
looked good on you, too.

09:42.520 --> 09:45.980
I just got a little excited
because I was happy to find out

09:45.980 --> 09:47.850
our clothing hobbies
were kind of the same.

09:49.020 --> 09:50.110
Sorry about that.

09:50.860 --> 09:52.860
Oh, no worries.

09:53.230 --> 09:55.570
All right, since the weather's nice,

09:55.820 --> 09:58.820
I'll make some bento and we can
eat that outside for lunch.

09:58.820 --> 10:00.070
Okay!

10:00.070 --> 10:06.330
<i>She herself didn't notice that she was outdone
within a minute by the oblivious Romeo.</i>

10:12.460 --> 10:17.170
<b>WITCH'S DELIVERY SERVICE</b>

10:13.210 --> 10:15.260
That's a pretty big delivery.

10:15.840 --> 10:19.760
It's all for me.
I asked Mom to send it to me.

10:19.760 --> 10:21.010
What's inside?

10:21.220 --> 10:23.390
It should just be manga.

10:23.390 --> 10:26.310
There's Kochikame Tokyo Beat Cops,
Golgo 13, and Oishinbo.

10:26.310 --> 10:28.390
Those all have a lot of books
in their series!

10:29.400 --> 10:30.900
TO MORIHITO

10:29.980 --> 10:30.900
A letter?

10:31.020 --> 10:32.730
It must be from my mom.

10:33.440 --> 10:35.860
From Ms. Ibuki, to me?

10:34.400 --> 10:36.400
TO MORIHITO

10:37.570 --> 10:40.160
<i>I'm sorry to ask so much of you.</i>

10:40.950 --> 10:42.490
<i>I thought about other options,</i>

10:42.490 --> 10:45.910
<i>but it's probably best
that you look after her for now.</i>

10:46.790 --> 10:49.920
<i>I'm currently living in a village
called Yuzenkyo.</i>

10:50.080 --> 10:52.420
<i>When witch hunts ravaged
other countries,</i>

10:52.420 --> 10:55.670
<i>witches sought refuge here, in Japan,
and made this their new holy land.</i>

10:55.880 --> 10:57.920
<i>This is where Nico
underwent her training.</i>

10:58.420 --> 11:00.760
<i>I chose to stay here</i>

11:00.760 --> 11:04.350
<i>because this is the best place
for me to raise my magical energy.</i>

11:04.930 --> 11:07.310
<i>Prophecies require a vast amount
of magic power,</i>

11:07.310 --> 11:10.940
<i>and for my current self, I can't really say
that I have a high success rate.</i>

11:11.770 --> 11:14.940
<i>In order to gain accurate information
regarding Nico's disaster,</i>

11:14.940 --> 11:17.190
<i>I will remain in these lands
and train harder.</i>

11:17.990 --> 11:20.910
<i>Until then, I ask that
you please protect Nico.</i>

11:20.910 --> 11:24.450
<i>Can you look after her studies,
and also keep track of her allowance?</i>

11:24.620 --> 11:27.830
<i>And please don't spoil her,
and scold her when necessary.</i>

11:27.830 --> 11:29.910
Seems like she's asking me to do a lot.

11:30.290 --> 11:33.960
<i>You've really helped her
a lot ever since you two were kids.</i>

11:34.420 --> 11:37.380
I had Moi help me
with my science project.

11:37.380 --> 11:40.720
Sheesh, you should try
to get things done on your own.

11:41.260 --> 11:43.800
Don't always be relying on Morihito.

11:44.510 --> 11:46.640
Thank you so much, Morihito.

11:50.680 --> 11:52.730
Moi, are you done?

11:53.150 --> 11:55.610
Can you help me carry these boxes?

11:55.810 --> 11:57.860
You should do things on your own!

11:58.070 --> 11:58.860
What?

11:58.860 --> 12:00.990
I won't spoil you! I'm gonna scold you!

12:00.990 --> 12:05.280
Damn it, he read Mom's letter,
so his sense of responsibility has gone up!

12:06.080 --> 12:09.620
A-All right fine, I'll carry it myself.

12:10.120 --> 12:10.960
Super Li—

12:10.960 --> 12:12.120
Don't you dare!

12:12.540 --> 12:15.080
You shouldn't use magic for this.

12:15.080 --> 12:18.250
Don't you remember the drawback that
happens and your personality gets heavy, too?

12:18.460 --> 12:23.550
Hold on, are you saying
you hate heavy women? So hurtful.

12:23.550 --> 12:25.260
You're already getting heavy-hearted!

12:25.640 --> 12:27.850
Don't rely on magic to make things easy.

12:27.850 --> 12:32.100
It's your own Kochikame and Golgo,
so you should carry it in yourself.

12:33.020 --> 12:35.400
But Golgo is Mom's...

12:38.190 --> 12:42.740
There's a spell that lets me carry them myself,
while also being more efficient!

12:43.820 --> 12:45.990
Doublit!

12:50.410 --> 12:51.790
There's two of them!

12:52.160 --> 12:53.040
So?

12:53.040 --> 12:54.160
Cool, right?

12:57.960 --> 12:59.300
But you're small.

13:00.000 --> 13:04.380
When that magic splits you into two,
does your size also become split as well?

13:04.380 --> 13:06.470
Okay, let's get started.

13:06.470 --> 13:08.430
Good idea, let's do this.

13:08.680 --> 13:12.060
Heave, and ho, and heave, and ho.

13:12.350 --> 13:14.390
Ugh, it's so heavy.

13:14.770 --> 13:15.690
Let me help you.

13:16.020 --> 13:17.810
Ready, and...

13:18.110 --> 13:19.730
Easy-peasy, easy-peasy.

13:19.730 --> 13:21.570
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Stop! That's so pointless!

13:21.820 --> 13:24.030
That's not more efficient!

13:24.150 --> 13:27.070
There're two of you, but you're still
only carrying one person's worth of boxes!

13:28.160 --> 13:30.370
Their intelligence
has also been split into two.

13:30.580 --> 13:32.620
Magic is so useful!

13:32.620 --> 13:35.290
Stop acting like you accomplished
something, you little idiots!

13:36.210 --> 13:38.080
Easy-peasy, easy-peasy.

13:38.420 --> 13:40.880
Easy-peasy, easy-peasy.

13:40.880 --> 13:42.590
Ugh, I have to keep my eyes on them.

13:43.710 --> 13:46.760
Hey, if we cast Doublit again,

13:46.760 --> 13:49.850
won't the two of us split
into two again and become four of us?

13:53.680 --> 13:55.100
- That's it!
- Stop it!

13:55.270 --> 13:57.060
Doublit!

13:58.400 --> 14:00.150
They're quarter-sized!

14:00.560 --> 14:03.190
Ready, and here we go!

14:03.190 --> 14:04.490
I'm telling you this is pointless!

14:04.900 --> 14:08.200
This spell is no good, no matter how many
times you split, it still adds up to one!

14:08.200 --> 14:09.160
Well, of course.

14:09.160 --> 14:12.740
If you can endlessly copy something, any food
and energy problems would instantly be resolved.

14:12.990 --> 14:15.250
I'll go, "Beep beep"!

14:15.250 --> 14:18.120
Then I'll go, "One, two, one, two."

14:18.460 --> 14:21.380
Then I'll go, "One, two, one, two," too!

14:21.500 --> 14:24.260
- Then I'll go, "One, two, one, two," too!
- Hurry up!

14:24.380 --> 14:26.470
- One, two!
- Beep, beep!

14:26.550 --> 14:28.680
- One, two!
- Beep, beep!

14:28.760 --> 14:30.760
- One, two!
- Beep, beep!

14:30.850 --> 14:32.760
- One, two!
- Beep, beep!

14:32.930 --> 14:34.770
All units...

14:34.850 --> 14:36.640
- Halt!
- Beep beep!

14:37.270 --> 14:38.270
What!

14:38.560 --> 14:40.690
It's fine, I'll just carry it!

14:41.650 --> 14:43.400
We finished so fast.

14:43.610 --> 14:45.400
So strong.

14:45.400 --> 14:47.610
It's an ogre moving company.

14:49.070 --> 14:52.240
Come on, quit horsing around
and get back to one person.

14:52.240 --> 14:53.870
Just a bit longer!

14:53.950 --> 14:55.910
Don't go outside the gate, okay?

14:55.910 --> 14:57.620
Okay!

14:57.620 --> 14:59.790
What am I, a preschool teacher?

15:00.420 --> 15:03.250
That's right, I haven't finished
reading the letter.

15:03.710 --> 15:06.710
<i>There's one more thing
I have to tell you.</i>

15:06.880 --> 15:09.430
<i>I've had a new prophecy.</i>

15:09.880 --> 15:11.300
<i>A new prophecy?</i>

15:11.760 --> 15:15.010
<i>Dogs and raindrops will bring disaster.</i>

15:15.310 --> 15:19.560
<i>Dogs and raindrops? From the rain?
What does this mean?</i>

15:20.480 --> 15:23.650
<i>Is getting attacked
by the dog the disaster? Wait...</i>

15:25.900 --> 15:27.940
Moi!

15:28.070 --> 15:29.030
Nico!

15:37.910 --> 15:38.870
Are you all right?

15:38.950 --> 15:42.250
Oh, I'm so sorry!
My Champ escaped his leash.

15:43.040 --> 15:45.840
I know that sometimes dogs can shake
their collars off from themselves.

15:46.380 --> 15:48.170
So I can overlook it this time.

15:49.380 --> 15:55.010
However, I hope you can overlook things
when the mask comes off the beast.

15:55.970 --> 15:58.430
I-I'm really, really sorry!

16:00.390 --> 16:03.270
That must've been scary.
Let's go back to normal, okay?

16:06.070 --> 16:08.480
Moi!

16:10.820 --> 16:12.150
I'm truly sorry.

16:12.660 --> 16:14.910
I got carried away, and...

16:15.240 --> 16:19.540
I split up into four and was having fun,
but you ended up getting hurt.

16:19.870 --> 16:21.210
It's fine, really.

16:21.910 --> 16:23.670
I'm glad you didn't get hurt.

16:24.420 --> 16:25.750
Yeah.

16:26.630 --> 16:29.800
Let me make some coffee.
And milk for me.

16:33.050 --> 16:38.180
<i>I cast magic on this glyph to disappear
when Nico's disaster has passed.</i>

16:38.760 --> 16:42.390
<i>This way, it'll be easy to tell
if the disaster has happened or not.</i>

16:43.390 --> 16:47.610
<i>It hasn't disappeared, so that means
the disaster wasn't that dog.</i>

16:48.360 --> 16:52.070
<i>Dog and raindrops.
What kind of disaster could it be?</i>

16:52.700 --> 16:55.280
<i>Will it happen on a rainy day?</i>

16:56.030 --> 16:57.780
<i>Just knowing that would help.</i>

16:58.450 --> 17:02.000
<i>From west Japan to the Kanto region,
the weather will begin to decline.</i>

17:02.370 --> 17:04.830
<i>It will continue to decline
from the evening as well.</i>

17:20.010 --> 17:24.940
<b>THE TWO FEELING
A LITTLE AWKWARD

AFTER HE SAW THE BACKSIDE</b>

17:25.020 --> 17:29.940
THE TWO FEELING A LITTLE AWKWARD

AFTER HE SAW THE BACKSIDE

17:30.500 --> 17:34.570
<b>LOST DOGS AND THE PATTER OF RAIN</b>

17:35.360 --> 17:38.030
Hurray, we got some Koshinoya yokan.

17:38.030 --> 17:40.700
Why did we have to come out
in the rain to buy these?

17:40.910 --> 17:45.750
I'm sorry. The best way to replenish
my magic power is by eating red beans.

17:45.830 --> 17:48.960
You could've stayed home, you know.

17:49.340 --> 17:51.710
But the prophecy... Cough, cough.

17:52.920 --> 17:54.970
It's nothing, let's hurry on home.

17:55.260 --> 17:56.130
Okay.

17:57.220 --> 17:59.220
<i>I probably shouldn't tell her
about the prophecy.</i>

17:59.550 --> 18:01.970
<i>I don't want her
to worry about anything.</i>

18:02.350 --> 18:05.980
But I wonder if it'll be better
to tell her about it.

18:06.230 --> 18:11.020
And so, there's this anime called
Wonder Ful-Ful, and it's such a cute anime.

18:06.890 --> 18:10.150
<i>When Nico's by herself,
the disaster might happen.</i>

18:10.150 --> 18:13.530
<i>I wish there was an informant who
I could work with in times of emergencies.</i>

18:11.020 --> 18:13.530
They have some collaboration cafes
going on right now,

18:13.530 --> 18:15.860
but would you be interested
in that kind of thing?

18:14.820 --> 18:18.700
<i>If that's the case, I can think of it
as a way of avoiding danger. But still...</i>

18:18.700 --> 18:22.030
What the heck? You aren't
even listening to what I'm saying.

18:22.030 --> 18:24.700
Oh, sorry about that.
What was it again?

18:24.700 --> 18:25.960
It's the anime about a dog—

18:25.960 --> 18:27.870
A dog?! What about them?

18:28.620 --> 18:30.130
Moi, you're scaring me.

18:30.130 --> 18:31.920
Oh, I'm sorry.

18:33.170 --> 18:34.800
So what were you talking about?

18:34.800 --> 18:36.010
Never mind!

18:36.880 --> 18:39.050
<i>Anyway, I have to be careful
on rainy days.</i>

18:39.550 --> 18:42.260
<i>If something happens,
I need to be able to protect Nico.</i>

18:43.600 --> 18:44.390
Nico.

18:46.270 --> 18:47.690
Come in under my umbrella.

18:55.690 --> 18:58.110
<i>Moi really made an explosive move.</i>

18:58.110 --> 19:01.160
<i>I'm really shocked that he'd suddenly
invite me under his umbrella.</i>

19:01.160 --> 19:03.530
<i>I wish someone could see us like this.</i>

19:03.530 --> 19:05.410
Huh? Hey, it's Nico.

19:05.410 --> 19:06.290
Oh, Kara.

19:06.580 --> 19:09.080
Huh? What? Are you two
sharing an umbrella?

19:09.080 --> 19:13.290
Come on, Nico, stop flirting
and come shopping with me.

19:13.900 --> 19:19.220
I'M SORRY, I CAN'T

19:15.500 --> 19:19.220
Don't you be mouthing, "I'm sorry, I can't,"
at me like that! How irritating!

19:30.640 --> 19:34.690
Huh? This isn't the way home.
Are we stopping by somewhere?

19:35.070 --> 19:35.860
Yeah.

19:45.280 --> 19:47.950
<i>This is definitely a confession of love!</i>

19:48.450 --> 19:49.080
Nico.

19:49.080 --> 19:50.370
Yes, I am ready.

19:50.370 --> 19:52.790
What? Hold this umbrella
and stand back.

19:52.790 --> 19:53.580
What?

19:54.210 --> 19:55.670
You suck at hiding. Come out.

19:56.130 --> 19:57.760
I know you've been following us.

19:57.760 --> 19:59.630
What? We were being followed?

19:59.630 --> 20:00.470
Yeah.

20:03.680 --> 20:05.470
Can't believe I have a fan already.

20:05.470 --> 20:06.890
Definitely not it.

20:08.430 --> 20:10.730
<i>This person is pretty good
at sneaking around.</i>

20:11.020 --> 20:12.600
<i>I doubt anybody but me
would've noticed.</i>

20:13.230 --> 20:16.360
<i>Is it you?
Is today the day of the disaster?</i>

20:16.940 --> 20:18.360
<i>Come on, show yourself.</i>

20:18.780 --> 20:20.110
<i>Is it someone I know?</i>

20:20.740 --> 20:22.360
<i>Or someone who knows me?</i>

20:23.030 --> 20:24.110
<i>Who the hell is that?</i>

20:25.490 --> 20:26.370
Really, who is that?

20:26.580 --> 20:27.740
It's Wonder Ful-Ful!

20:27.740 --> 20:28.740
The mystery deepens!

20:29.080 --> 20:31.910
It's the main character
from an anime I like.

20:32.670 --> 20:34.380
I don't care about
the character on the mask.

20:35.040 --> 20:36.920
<i>Dog, and raindrops.</i>

20:37.630 --> 20:39.210
Who could this be?

20:41.510 --> 20:45.390
<i>He looks like he's slumping,
but there's no openings. If anything...</i>

20:46.300 --> 20:48.220
<i>You're ready to go, aren't you?</i>

20:54.520 --> 20:58.150
<i>He's fast! But I'm still stronger.
I can win.</i>

20:59.690 --> 21:00.610
A special baton?

21:08.080 --> 21:09.870
- Moi!
- Stay back!

21:10.490 --> 21:12.870
<i>I let my guard down. This guy...</i>

21:13.370 --> 21:14.960
<i>can control the wind.</i>

21:16.040 --> 21:18.750
If you're attacking me, then
that means you're Nico's enemy.

21:19.040 --> 21:20.630
So I won't go easy on you.

21:20.960 --> 21:23.670
Ogre Qigong Fighting Style, Ogre Wisp.

21:26.640 --> 21:29.100
That was a feint technique
that shows you an illusion.

21:29.600 --> 21:33.520
Sorry Poochie,
but instead of fighting it out seriously,

21:33.520 --> 21:36.060
it's more important
to find out who you are.

21:36.060 --> 21:38.110
Come on now, just let me see your face.

21:39.440 --> 21:40.230
You're...

21:41.860 --> 21:42.780
a stranger?

21:42.780 --> 21:43.740
Kan!

21:47.530 --> 21:49.200
Nico!

21:49.330 --> 21:51.040
It was you, Kan?

21:51.120 --> 21:53.120
Took you long enough!

21:53.120 --> 21:55.620
You should've known it was me
by the way I fight.

21:55.620 --> 21:56.830
You know him, Nico?

21:57.170 --> 22:00.250
Yeah! Let me introduce you.
This is Kan!

22:00.250 --> 22:01.460
Still a stranger!

22:01.920 --> 22:06.220
Kan is a tengu who lives
on the mountain where I trained.

22:06.340 --> 22:07.720
A tengu?

22:09.720 --> 22:14.230
Sorry about that, Ogre,
but I was just testing your skills.

22:14.980 --> 22:16.940
Kanshi Kazamatsuri.

22:17.390 --> 22:19.980
I came here to protect Nico, too.

22:20.980 --> 22:23.190
I'm her crow familiar.

23:57.790 --> 24:00.290
The masked man
finally appeared before us.

24:00.290 --> 24:01.170
That's Kan.

24:01.170 --> 24:03.710
And behind that mask was a crow familiar!

24:03.710 --> 24:04.920
His name is Kan.

24:04.920 --> 24:06.630
Who could this man be?

24:06.630 --> 24:07.920
It's Kan!

24:07.920 --> 24:09.550
Next episode,
"The Death of Joey Wheeler."

24:07.920 --> 24:11.970
NEXT EPISODE
KANSHI KAZAMATSURI, THE TENGU

24:09.550 --> 24:10.970
Who's that!
